{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgAG1dPdsVY8Fruz1jpcr","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I fixed `Hijack()` so it fails only after body bytes have been written, not as soon as the headers go out. Tests pass (`go test ./...`).\n\n- **The bug:** `Hijack()` in `response_writer.go` refused to run once `Written()` was true. That is already the case once headers are sent (`size == 0`). Websocket libraries such as `github.com/coder/websocket` send headers and then hijack, so they got the error.\n- **The fix:** the check is now `w.size > 0`. Hijacking works before anything is written and after headers only. It still fails after body data. I also changed the error text to \"gin: response body already written\" to match.\n- **Test:** I added a \"hijack after header write should succeed\" case to `TestResponseWriterHijackAfterWrite`.\n\nI haven't committed anything. I didn't test against a real websocket library, only the mock hijacker in the existing test."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":178,"cache_read_input_tokens":34318,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":178,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":7,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"4509e96e-dd8b-4051-8a4d-de601153ec48","uuid":"a1174ff5-e8c0-4c73-bbf3-9fccd438235f","timestamp":"2026-10-18T19:32:09.472Z","request_id":"req_011CgAG1dBUtsVvGEG9otw54"}
