k, so they got the error.\n- **The fix:** the check is now `w.size > 0`. Hijacking works before anything is written and after headers only. It still fails after body data. I also changed the error text to \"gin: response body already written\" to match.\n- **Test:** I added a \"hijack after header write should succeed\" case to `TestResponseWriterHijackAfterWrite`.\n\nI haven't committed anything. I didn't test against a real websocket library, only the mock hijacker in the existing test.","ttft_ms":5412,"type":"result","duration_ms":24607,"uuid":"518177e4-c079-4f70-a574-5520b78117b6","ttft_stream_ms":2357,"time_to_request_ms":142,"first_content_frame_ms":2357,"queued_turn_count":0,"result_index":0}
